            <ArticleTitle>Localized Lysosome Exocytosis Helps Breach Tissue Barriers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377-378</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1534-5807(17)30909-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.devcel.2017.11.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cell invasion across basement membrane barriers is important in both normal development and cancer metastasis. In this issue of Developmental Cell, Naegeli et al. (2017) identify a mechanism for breaching basement membranes. Localized lysosome exocytosis fuels generation of large, invasive cellular protrusions that expand tiny basement membrane openings.</AbstractText>
